      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should probably sync this with https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/1371811.\n* The other change uses sanitized: { \u003csanitizer name\u003e: { src: }}}\n* The other change appends sanitized paths to the regular paths, and provides a special \"none\" sanitized option when you need exclusive-or. This matches the behavior of \"arch:\" and \"target:\" properties.\n\nI\u0027m not sure which approach is better. Neither works well with non-exclusive sanitizers (ex. cfi + integer).\n\nIt looks like this assignment will override all properties, not just \"src\". For example, in\nvendor_snapshot_static {\n    name: \"libfoo\",\n    src: \"libfoo.a\",\n    export_flags: \"-zzzz\",\n    cfi: {\n        src: \"libfoo.cfi.a\",\n    },\n}\nwill the value of \"export_flags\" be lost in the cfi variant?",
